# UITK palette colors (Grid Dungeon)

**Authority:** `Assets/UI/Settings/Themes/GridDungeonPaletteDark.uss` (default) and `GridDungeonPaletteLight.uss` — imported by theme TSS assets → `GamePanelSettings`. Runtime swap: `GridDungeonUiThemeSystem`.

C# mirror for 3D / fades: `GridDungeon.Runtime.Characters.GridDungeonPalette` (`Assets/Scripts/Runtime/Characters/GridDungeonUiPalette.cs`).

## Rule

| Layer | Color source |
|-------|----------------|
| **Player HUD / overlays** (`Assets/UI/Screens/**`) | `var(--gd-*)` only — **no** inline `rgb()`, `rgba()`, or `#hex` |
| **New / changed tokens** | Add to **both** `GridDungeonPaletteDark.uss` and `GridDungeonPaletteLight.uss` (same `--gd-*` names), then reference from screen USS |
| **Editor tools** (`Assets/UI/Editor/**`) | Exempt — may use editor-skin literals until a dedicated editor palette exists |
| **Design mirror** (`Assets/UI/Editor/DesignMirror/**`) | Prefer palette vars when mirroring production screens; literals OK for throwaway sandbox chrome |

## Token naming

- **Swatches:** `--gd-swatch-01` … `--gd-swatch-10`
- **Neutrals:** `--gd-base`, `--gd-surface`, `--gd-chrome`, `--gd-ink`, `--gd-muted`, alpha variants (`--gd-base-a78`, …)
- **Semantic:** `--gd-accent`, `--gd-threat`, `--gd-ally`, `--gd-protocol`, `--gd-focus-bg`, …
- **Feature-specific:** `--gd-map-*`, `--gd-story-*`, `--gd-bar-*` — add when a screen needs a role not covered by neutrals/semantic

Reuse existing tokens before adding new ones. If the literal already matches a token value, swap — do not duplicate under a second name.

## Allowed in screen USS without a token

- `var(--gd-transparent)` instead of `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)` for explicit clears
- Non-color properties (`px`, `flex`, `translate`, …)

## Agent / PR checklist

- [ ] Touched screen USS uses `var(--gd-*)` for every color property (including `border-*-color`, `-unity-background-image-tint-color`, `text-shadow` color)
- [ ] New colors land in dark + light palette USS with the same semantic token name
- [ ] 3D / C# color that must match HUD → extend `GridDungeonPalette` C# mirror when adding a runtime-facing token
- [ ] Editor-only USS left unchanged unless the task scopes editor UI

## Examples

```css
/* ❌ BAD — literal in screen USS */
.hud-overlay__title {
    color: rgb(232, 234, 237);
}

/* ✅ GOOD */
.hud-overlay__title {
    color: var(--gd-ink);
}
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD — one-off alpha in feature file */
.map-view__marker--foe {
    background-color: rgba(247, 37, 133, 0.98);
}

/* ✅ GOOD — semantic alias in palette, threat swatch underneath */
/* GridDungeonPaletteDark.uss: --gd-map-foe-marker: var(--gd-threat-a98); */
.map-view__marker--foe {
    background-color: var(--gd-map-foe-marker);
}
```

